# A2/A2.1/A2_06_train_travel.letz
# Source: PDF slide decks "L4 (Part 1)/(Part 2) a21convlotsmanmeli.pdf" (A2.1, Lektioun 4:
# Gespréicher op der Gare an am Kleedergeschäft féiere kënnen).
# Slide text was baked into the raster; transcribed from rendered pages, then every
# lemma verified against LOD.
# Split from A2.07 (the clothes-shop half of the same deck) to keep both near the
# 40-60 Element sizing target.
# The deck's separable verbs are taught as infinitives; their split forms
# (`Ech klammen an`) appear in the sentences.
# Grammar focus: travel-register prepositions and contracted forms; separable-verb
# prefixes in main clauses; root-changing second- and third-person singular forms.

@lesson A2.06 "Train Travel"

# --- Tickets & station ---
@word de Billjee = the ticket
@word d'Billjeeën = the tickets
@word d'Gare = the railway station
@word den Départ = the departure
@word d'Reservatioun = the reservation
@word de Spezialtarif = the special fare
@word de Virdeel = the advantage

# --- Verbs of travel ---
@word fortfueren = to depart by vehicle
@word ëmklammen = to change trains
@word eraklammen = to board
@word erausklammen = to get off
@word fortfléien = to depart by plane
@word kaschten = to cost
@word widderhuelen = to repeat

# --- Describing the journey ---
@word pünktlech = punctually
@word Lount dat sech? = Is it worth it?

@sentence
@lu Wéi vill kascht e Billjee fir op Budapest?
@en How much does a ticket to Budapest cost?
@distractor-en platform
@distractor-en reservation
@distractor-lu Quai
@distractor-lu Reservatioun

@sentence
@lu Gëtt et e Spezialtarif?
@en Is there a special fare?
@distractor-en advantage
@distractor-en platform
@distractor-lu Virdeel
@distractor-lu Quai

@sentence
@lu Um wéi vill Auer fiert den Zuch fort?
@en At what time does the train depart?
@distractor-en arrives
@distractor-en platform
@distractor-lu ukënnt
@distractor-lu Quai

@sentence
@lu Den Départ ass um siwen Auer.
@en The departure is at seven o'clock.
@distractor-en arrival
@distractor-en eight
@distractor-lu Arrivée
@distractor-lu aacht

@sentence
@lu Op wéi engem Quai fiert den Zuch fort?
@en From which platform does the train depart?
@distractor-en station
@distractor-en arrives
@distractor-lu Gare
@distractor-lu ukënnt

@sentence
@lu Den Zuch kënnt um eng Auer un.
@en The train arrives at one o'clock.
@distractor-en departs
@distractor-en two
@distractor-lu fortfiert
@distractor-lu zwou

@sentence
@lu D'Arrivée zu Budapest ass owes.
@en The arrival in Budapest is in the evening.
@distractor-en departure
@distractor-en morning
@distractor-lu Départ
@distractor-lu moies

@sentence
@lu Wéi oft muss ech ëmklammen?
@en How often do I have to change trains?
@distractor-en board
@distractor-en platform
@distractor-lu eraklammen
@distractor-lu Quai

@sentence
@lu Dir musst zu Bréissel ëmklammen.
@en You have to change trains in Brussels.
@distractor-en board
@distractor-en station
@distractor-lu eraklammen
@distractor-lu Gare

@sentence
@lu Den Zuch ass haut immens voll.
@en The train is extremely full today.
@distractor-en empty
@distractor-en tomorrow
@distractor-lu eidel
@distractor-lu muer

@sentence
@lu Ech muss an de Waggon eraklammen.
@en I have to board the carriage.
@distractor-en get off
@distractor-en platform
@distractor-lu erausklammen
@distractor-lu Quai

@sentence
@lu Dir musst op der nächster Statioun erausklammen.
@en You have to get off at the next station.
@distractor-en board
@distractor-en first
@distractor-lu eraklammen
@distractor-lu éischter

@sentence
@lu De Fliger flitt pünktlech fort.
@en The plane departs punctually.
@distractor-en train
@distractor-en late
@distractor-lu Zuch
@distractor-lu spéit

@sentence
@lu Ech géif gär eng Reservatioun maachen.
@en I would like to make a reservation.
@distractor-en repeat
@distractor-en platform
@distractor-lu widderhuelen
@distractor-lu Quai

@sentence
@lu Den Zuch fiert op Lëtzebuerg.
@en The train goes to Luxembourg.
@distractor-en arrives
@distractor-en station
@distractor-lu kënnt
@distractor-lu Gare

@sentence
@lu Wéi een Dag fiert den Zuch fort?
@en On which day does the train depart?
@distractor-en arrives
@distractor-en hour
@distractor-lu ukënnt
@distractor-lu Auer

@sentence
@lu Déi éischt Klass kascht méi wéi déi zweet Klass.
@en The first class costs more than the second class.
@distractor-en less
@distractor-en third
@distractor-lu manner
@distractor-lu drëtt

@sentence
@lu Ech stinn all Dag um siwen Auer op.
@en I get up at seven o'clock every day.
@distractor-en eight
@distractor-en evening
@distractor-lu aacht
@distractor-lu owes

@sentence
@lu Wéini stees du op?
@en When do you get up?
@distractor-en where
@distractor-en board
@distractor-lu Wou
@distractor-lu klamms

@sentence
@lu Ech fuere muer mam Zuch fort.
@en I depart by train tomorrow.
@distractor-en today
@distractor-en bus
@distractor-lu haut
@distractor-lu Bus

@sentence
@lu Dat hänkt dovun of.
@en That depends.
@distractor-en costs
@distractor-en arrives
@distractor-lu kascht
@distractor-lu kënnt


# --- Timetables & connections ---
@sentence
@lu Den Départ vum Zuch ass op dem Quai dräi A.
@en The train's departure is from platform three A.
@distractor-en arrival
@distractor-en four
@distractor-lu Arrivée
@distractor-lu véier

@sentence
@lu An um wéi vill Auer kënnt den Zuch un?
@en And at what time does the train arrive?
@distractor-en departs
@distractor-en platform
@distractor-lu fortfiert
@distractor-lu Quai

@sentence
@lu D'Arrivée zu Budapest ass owes um eenanzwanzeg Auer zwanzeg.
@en The arrival in Budapest is at twenty past nine in the evening.
@distractor-en departure
@distractor-en morning
@distractor-lu Départ
@distractor-lu moies

@sentence
@lu Dir musst zwee Mol ëmklammen, ee Mol zu Frankfurt an ee Mol zu Wien.
@en You have to change trains twice, once in Frankfurt and once in Vienna.
@distractor-en board
@distractor-en station
@distractor-lu eraklammen
@distractor-lu Gare

@sentence
@lu Den Zuch fiert den éischten August fort.
@en The train departs on the first of August.
@distractor-en arrives
@distractor-en September
@distractor-lu kënnt
@distractor-lu September

@sentence
@lu Den Zuch kënnt um uechtzéng Auer drësseg un.
@en The train arrives at half past six.
@distractor-en departs
@distractor-en seven
@distractor-lu fortfiert
@distractor-lu siwen

@sentence
@lu Den Ticket kascht eenanzwanzeg Euro.
@en The ticket costs twenty-one euros.
@distractor-en departure
@distractor-en twenty-two
@distractor-lu Départ
@distractor-lu zweeanzwanzeg

@sentence
@lu Sidd Dir Student oder hutt Dir eng BahnCard?
@en Are you a student or do you have a BahnCard?
@distractor-en ticket
@distractor-en reservation
@distractor-lu Billjee
@distractor-lu Reservatioun

@sentence
@lu Wou fiert den Zuch?
@en Where does the train go?
@distractor-en when
@distractor-en arrives
@distractor-lu Wéini
@distractor-lu kënnt

# --- Separable verbs in main clauses ---
@sentence
@lu Du fiers muer mam Zuch fort.
@en You depart by train tomorrow.
@distractor-en today
@distractor-en bus
@distractor-lu haut
@distractor-lu Bus

@sentence
@lu Hie fiert um siwen Auer fort.
@en He departs at seven o'clock.
@distractor-en arrives
@distractor-en eight
@distractor-lu kënnt
@distractor-lu aacht

@sentence
@lu Du kënns um Quai dräi un.
@en You arrive at platform three.
@distractor-en depart
@distractor-en four
@distractor-lu fiert
@distractor-lu véier

@sentence
@lu Si kënnt owes zu Budapest un.
@en She arrives in Budapest in the evening.
@distractor-en departs
